tags: network-rate

A limit of the node: the most bytes for each second that the node relays through ServiceTunnel, for all the clients together.

The value is an integer in bytes/second. Example: 104857600. The node slows the traffic to stay at or below the value.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=network-rate
per=all the clients of the node together
rule=The node slows the traffic to stay at or below the value.
scope=none
unit=bytes/second
